    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Turn new RSS posts into a weekly NotebookLM podcast\n\nEvery Monday this workflow reads an RSS feed, takes the newest posts and turns them into one **NotebookLM Audio Overview**, the two-host podcast, as an audio file ready for the next node. It runs on your own **Gemini Notebook** (formerly NotebookLM) account through the [useapi.net Gemini Notebook API](https://useapi.net/docs/api-gemini-notebook-v1). Google's own NotebookLM API is Enterprise-only (Google Cloud licenses).\n\n### Who's it for\nNewsletter writers, community managers and teams who want an audio digest of a blog, a news feed or a release log without doing it by hand.\n\n### How it works\n1. A schedule starts the run every Monday at 7:00.\n2. **Read feed** fetches the feed. **Newest posts** keeps the ones from the last 7 days, at most 5. No new posts, no episode. Posts without a date are skipped, so a feed without dates makes no episode.\n3. The workflow creates a notebook, adds the post links as sources and waits until Google has processed them.\n4. It generates the Audio Overview, polls the job until it is done (usually 3 to 10 minutes), and downloads the `.m4a`.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Create a useapi.net account and [API token](https://useapi.net/docs/start-here/setup-useapi), then connect your Google account with the [Gemini Notebook setup](https://useapi.net/docs/start-here/setup-gemini-notebook).\n2. Create a **Header Auth** credential. Name: `Authorization`. Value: `Bearer <your API token>`.\n3. Select the credential on the six HTTP Request nodes.\n4. Put your feed in **Feed settings**, click **Execute workflow** to try it, then publish (activate) the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\n- A useapi.net subscription ($15/month flat).\n- A Google account with access to Gemini Notebook.\n\n### How to customize\n- Change the day and hour in the schedule, and `lookbackDays` to match.\n- Set `format`, `length` and `language` in **Feed settings**.\n- Add a Google Drive, Telegram or podcast-host node after **Download audio**.",
        "width": 440,
        "height": 950
      },
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -480,
        -60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Feed settings\nYour feed URL, the episode name, how many posts and how many days back. Leave `email` empty unless you want a specific Google account.",
        "width": 240,
        "height": 200,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Feed settings note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        160,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Newest posts\nKeeps the posts published within `lookbackDays`, newest first, up to `maxPosts`, and joins their links into one episode.",
        "width": 240,
        "height": 200,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Newest posts note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        600,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Sources first\nGoogle fetches and indexes every link before it can talk about them, so the workflow checks the notebook every 10 seconds until each source is `ready` (or `error`, which it skips).",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 150,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Sources note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1060,
        500
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Audio Overview\nGeneration is asynchronous: start the job, wait, check, and loop until it is `completed` or `failed`. The finished job lists its files. The download link needs your token, so the last HTTP Request node fetches it with the same credential.",
        "width": 1120,
        "height": 150,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Audio note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1960,
        400
      ]
    }
  ],
